Title: Ask AROS for an 8 MiB main stack
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: The main task overflowed its stack while building the UI (Software Failure 0x8100000E, Shell default stack).
Change: Define __stack = 8 MiB; AROS start-up code gives the main task at least that much.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: candidate
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110); LibreSprite starts on nightly 20261113 (pool v1-1, 2026-11-16)
Removal: None planned.
---
diff --git a/src/main/main.cpp b/src/main/main.cpp
index af7eaec20369c80e1024a33495ce001c38f05e31..80e28064578f2ec26c141913888a859bddba6dc1 100644
--- a/src/main/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main/main.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,12 @@
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
 #endif
+
+#ifdef __AROS__
+// AROS startup code reads __stack and gives the main task at least this much
+// stack; a Shell's default (often 256 KiB) is far too small for the UI.
+extern "C" { unsigned long __stack = 8 * 1024 * 1024; }
+#endif
 #ifdef EMSCRIPTEN
 #define LIFETIME static
 #else
